Package: zumime
Title: Media Type Detection from Bytes and File Names
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Apache Software Foundation", role = "cph",
           comment = "copyright holder of the httpd mime.types file the extension table is generated from; see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
  )
Description: Tells what a file is from its first bytes and from its name,
    with no system library. Implements the 'WHATWG' 'MIME' Sniffing
    Standard <https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/> over raw vectors and
    paths, inspects containers ('ZIP' entry names, 'ISO' base media
    brands, 'RIFF', 'EBML', 'Ogg', 'OLE2' directories) and recognises the
    data formats R users hold, such as 'RDS', 'Parquet', 'SQLite' and
    'Stata'. Every type has a parent ending at 'application/octet-stream',
    and an extension table generated from the 'IANA' media types registry
    and the 'Apache' 'httpd' type map answers from the name. One call
    reports both answers, whether they agree, and whether a file is
    compressed, encrypted or truncated.
